WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.601
Analysis tools help turn collected evidence into understandable findings.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:12.709
Log viewers and search tools allow analysts to filter large event sets, compare sources, and build timelines.

00:00:12.709 --> 00:00:23.445
Timeline tools can combine file system metadata, event logs, browser history, EDR records, and other artifacts so analysts can see activity in sequence.

00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:31.991
The value is not the tool interface; it is the ability to answer investigation questions with supporting evidence.

00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:40.975
Forensic suites may help with disk images, file systems, deleted files, browser artifacts, registry hives, user activity, and reporting.

00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:49.958
Registry viewers can support Windows investigations by exposing autoruns, user activity, mounted devices, service configuration, and other system state.

00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:59.819
Memory analysis tools can help identify running processes, network connections, loaded modules, suspicious handles, and other volatile evidence captured during acquisition.

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:05.735
Packet analysis and network tools are useful when the question involves communication.

00:01:05.735 --> 00:01:12.966
They may help analysts understand connections, protocols, session timing, DNS lookups, and data movement patterns.

00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:25.017
Malware triage tools can support safe, high-level analysis of suspicious files, such as hashes, metadata, strings, import tables, signatures, and sandbox-style observations in an approved environment.

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:32.686
The goal is to inform response, not to perform unnecessary deep reverse engineering for every case.

00:01:32.686 --> 00:01:36.849
Hash and metadata utilities are simple but important.

00:01:36.849 --> 00:01:41.451
They support identification, comparison, integrity checks, and evidence tracking.

00:01:41.451 --> 00:01:47.367
When building the toolkit, choose analysis tools by task rather than hype.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:53.283
A popular tool that does not answer your question is just noise.

00:01:53.283 --> 00:01:59.637
A boring tool that reliably parses the artifact you need can be essential.

00:01:59.637 --> 00:02:03.362
Tool selection should follow the investigation objective.
